//
// AN UNCOVERED VARIANT-AND-ARGUMENT PAIR IS REFUSED NAMING THE PAIR (`@FR-Disp-Exhaustive`
// crossed with `@FR-Disp-Applicable`).  `eb(XFire, integer = 10)` and `eb(XIce, integer = 20)`
// cover an `XEnt` argument for every variant when the second argument is an integer or omitted;
// a `text` second argument is taken by neither member (Disp-Applicable: `text` does not satisfy
// `integer`), so the call is not covered for any variant, and the refusal is at compile time —
// no run-time "no applicable method" path.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; refused as the rule says, interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the pair and the declared members.
// HOLDS: `a-covered-call-is-covered-for-every-variant-and-every-omitted-default` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `eb(XEnt, text)` has no definition for the pair (XFire, text)

enum XEnt { XFire { n: integer }, XIce { n: integer } }

fn eb(e: XFire, k: integer = 10) -> text { "fire {e.n} {k}" }
fn eb(e: XIce, k: integer = 20) -> text { "ice {e.n} {k}" }

fn main() {
  x: XEnt = XFire { n: 1 };
  println(eb(x, "t"));
}
